# OS
.DS_Store

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Private working material — deliberately not published.
#
# This repository is public and is the source of the robustmargin package on PyPI.
# The planning documents, the agent and tooling setup, and the internal review log
# stay local: they remain on disk and fully usable, and are never committed.
#
# None of them has ever been committed or pushed, so there is no history to purge.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Claude Code setup: agent definitions, skills, hook wiring, scratch
.claude/

# Repo tooling that references the above. The CI workflow is the exception: it is
# committed so GitHub Actions runs (owner decision 2026-09-12, resolving review R4
# option 1). `.github/*` rather than `.github/` — git cannot re-include a path
# whose parent directory is excluded. CODEOWNERS is committed too, so GitHub can
# request the code owner's review on every PR. The PR template is committed so GitHub
# pre-fills every PR description with it, including PRs opened from the web UI.
.github/*
!.github/workflows/
!.github/CODEOWNERS
!.github/pull_request_template.md

# Project instructions for Claude Code
CLAUDE.md

# Planning, architecture, consumer contract, statistics index, review log,
# and owner decision records. PROVENANCE.md is the exception: it carries the
# zeta-bench attribution that Apache-2.0 §4 expects to travel with the package
# (decision 0002), so it is committed (owner decision 2026-09-12).
docs/*
!docs/PROVENANCE.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Keeping CLAUDE.md and docs/ out of the repository is permanent, not a step to
# revisit before publishing: the repository is already public.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

